<DefaultData Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[0,2000,0]]]>
</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="TIMER">
<DataValueMember Name="PRE" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="2000"/>
<DataValueMember Name="ACC" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="TT" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="DN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[FanucRobot: Runs a sequence that handles starting, stopping, pausing, etc. a Fanuc robot using the PNS interface via UOP (user operator panel) signals.

To Use: 
- Place on a rung that runs every scan
- Create a SeqCtrl variable and set or map the mode and disableHmiStart variables in the same way used to set up a SeqCtrl AOI.
- Input/Map the robot's UI and UO signals 
- Create or map an existing allowable alarm codes array (see FanucAlarmLookup AOI documentation)
- Input the current robot last alarm string


Sequence Faults:
Bit 0: Robot did not reset during running
Bit 1: Robot did not stop (via CSTOP)
Bit 2: Cmd Enable UO is not on
Bit 3: System Ready UO is not on
Bit 4: Program number select took too long
Bit 5: Program number echo did not match
Bit 6: Program already running
Bit 7: Robot did not reset during restart
Bit 8: Robot did not restart
Bit 9: Robot aborted itself
Bit 10: Robot alarm not recoverable. Robot aborted
Bit 11: Robot did not hold. Aborting.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Prescan  /////////
i.e. Robot IO Mapping


///   IO Mapping   ///

Set imstop, sfspd, and enable on so the robot can run]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTE(robotUI.IMSTP) ,OTE(robotUI.SFSPD) ,OTE(robotUI.enable) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Auto-reset the hold (pause) signal if it is off and the robot has stopped running a program]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(robotUI.hold)XIO(robotUO.prgRunning)OTL(robotUI.hold);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Pulse the Reset Output to the robot and reset any seq faults upon request]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(resetRobotFault)[TON(faultResetTimer,?,?) ,ONS(ons.7) MOVE(0,seq.fault) ,XIC(faultResetTimer.TT) OTE(robotUI.faultReset) ,XIC(faultResetTimer.DN) OTU(resetRobotFault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Pulse the Start Output]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(startRobot)[TON(startTimer,?,?) ,XIC(startTimer.TT) OTE(robotUI.start) ,XIC(startTimer.DN) OTU(startRobot) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[faulted status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(robotUO.fault) ,XIC(seq.faulted) ]OTE(faulted);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[///   Sequence Commands   ///

Abort if the robot stops itself (once the robot has been started) or if it pauses and robot holds are not enabled

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(seq.running) XIO(enableRobotHold) XIO(robotUO.prgRunning) XIC(robotUO.prgPaused) ONS(ons.3) ,XIO(robotUO.prgRunning) XIO(robotUO.prgPaused) ONS(ons.6) XIO(seq.aborted) XIO(seq.aborting) XIO(seq.complete) NE(seq.currentStep,130) OTL(seq.fault.9) ]OTL(seq.cmdAbort);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Pause Command

If enabled, pause this program if the robot holds (paused) itself after the robot is running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(seq.running)EQ(seq.currentStep,300)XIC(enableRobotHold)XIO(robotUO.prgRunning)XIC(robotUO.prgPaused)ONS(ons.4)OTL(seq.cmdPause);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If robot pauses itself due to a fault, check that the fault is allowed. If not, abort.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(seq.paused)ONS(ons.5)XIC(robotUO.fault)[FanucAlarmLookup(alarmLookup,allowableAlarms,robotLastAlarm) ,XIO(alarmLookup.recoverableAlarm) OTL(seq.fault.10) OTL(seq.cmdAbort) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Sequence Status and Control   /////////]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SeqCtrl(seq,mode,disableHmiStart);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   RUNNING   /////////

Steps reserved for future use]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,0)MOVE(100,seq.nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[reset the CStop (abort) bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,100)[OTU(robotUI.cstop) ,MOVE(110,seq.nextStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset any robot faults. Abort if it doesn't reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,110)[XIC(robotUO.fault) [ONS(ons.0) OTL(resetRobotFault) ,TON(robotFaultResetTimeout1,?,?) ,XIC(robotFaultResetTimeout1.DN) OTL(seq.fault.0) OTL(seq.cmdAbort) ] ,XIO(robotUO.fault) MOVE(120,seq.nextStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Check if the robot is running a program. If it is, jump past PNS call.

If the program is paused, abort it so that it can be reset via the PNS call.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,120)[XIC(robotUO.prgRunning) MOVE(300,seq.nextStep) ,XIO(robotUO.prgRunning) [XIO(robotUO.prgPaused) MOVE(200,seq.nextStep) ,XIC(robotUO.prgPaused) [OTL(robotUI.cstop) ,MOVE(130,seq.nextStep) ] ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Wait for the current program to abort]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,130)[XIO(robotUO.prgRunning) XIO(robotUO.prgPaused) [OTU(robotUI.cstop) ,MOVE(200,seq.nextStep) ] ,XIC(robotUI.cstop) TON(cycleStopTimeout,?,?) ,XIC(cycleStopTimeout.DN) OTL(seq.fault.1) OTL(seq.cmdAbort) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Start the robot

Run the PNS Routine to start the robot's main program]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,200)[FanucPNS(PNS,progNumber,robotUI,robotUO) ,XIC(PNS.done) MOVE(300,seq.nextStep) ,XIC(PNS.faulted) BTD(PNS.fault,0,seq.fault,2,5) OTL(seq.cmdAbort) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Robot Running

Robot should run continously and interact with other programs for whatever process(es) need to happen. 
This program will never go to complete but instead will mimic the robot state with abort or hold.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,300)NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   COMPLETE   /////////

Step 2000. Waiting for start cmd
Note: This program should NEVER reach this state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Pausing   /////////

Pause the robot with the hold UO bit. If the robot doesn't respond, abort.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,3000)[OTU(robotUI.hold) ,XIC(robotUO.prgPaused) MOVE(4000,seq.nextStep) ,XIO(robotUO.prgPaused) TON(holdTimeout,?,?) ,XIC(holdTimeout.DN) OTL(seq.fault.11) OTL(seq.cmdAbort) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Paused   /////////

Step 4000: Robot Paused. Wait for restart command.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Restarting    /////////]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,5000)MOVE(5100,seq.nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset any robot faults again]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,5100)[XIC(robotUO.fault) [ONS(ons.1) OTL(resetRobotFault) ,TON(robotFaultResetTimeout2,?,?) ,XIC(robotFaultResetTimeout2.DN) OTL(seq.fault.7) OTL(seq.cmdAbort) ] ,XIO(robotUO.fault) MOVE(5110,seq.nextStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Restart the robot program by setting the "start" output and returning to the last known step in this program]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,5110)[ONS(ons.2) OTL(startRobot) ,XIC(robotUO.prgRunning) MOVE(300,seq.nextStep) ,TON(robotRestartTimeout,?,?) ,XIC(robotRestartTimeout.DN) OTL(seq.fault.8) MOVE(3000,seq.nextStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   ABORTING   /////////

Set the cycle stop output and wait for the robot program to abort (not paused and not running)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(seq.currentStep,6000)[[XIC(robotUO.prgRunning) ,XIC(robotUO.prgPaused) ] OTL(robotUI.cstop) ,XIO(robotUO.prgRunning) XIO(robotUO.prgPaused) [OTU(robotUI.cstop) ,MOVE(7000,seq.nextStep) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   ABORTED   /////////

Step 7000: Robot program stopped. Waiting for start command]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
<Tags>
<Tag Name="ALLOWABLE_ALARMS" TagType="Base" DataType="robotAlarmCode" Dimensions="20" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[[0,'$00$00$00$00$00$00$00$00'],[8,'SRVO-003'],[8,'SYST-043'],[8,'SYST-045'],[8,'SRVO-408'],[8,'SRVO-407'
		],[8,'SRVO-002'],[8,'SRVO-001'],[8,'SRVO-004'],[8,'SRVO-007'],[8,'SRVO-199'],[8,'SRVO-233'],[8,'SYST-034'],[0,'$00$00$00$00$00$00$00$00'
		],[0,'$00$00$00$00$00$00$00$00'],[0,'$00$00$00$00$00$00$00$00'],[0,'$00$00$00$00$00$00$00$00'
		],[0,'$00$00$00$00$00$00$00$00'],[0,'$00$00$00$00$00$00$00$00'],[0,'$00$00$00$00$00$00$00$00'
		]]]]>
</Data>
