<Routines>
<Routine Name="Main" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(RobotExample,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="RobotExample" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Fanuc Generic IO Mapping and Control Example]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Example Program for Mapping Generic Robot IO and for using the FanucRobotAOI

Replace ShopRobot with the names of your Ethernet Module and Robot Tag
Not valid if you don't use the generic robot IO config of:
Input: 260 bytes
Output: 52 bytes
Config: 0 bytes

It is also suggested to update the member names of the tags in the GenericRobot UDTs to match your application. The mapping should still work the same, however.

DELETE THIS RUNG WHEN DONE READING]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/// Map IO from Ethernet Module to Tags ///

Copy Inputs]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(ShopRobot:I.Data[0],ShopRobot.IN,1)COP(ShopRobot:I.Data[0],ShopRobot.IN,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copy Outputs
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(ShopRobot.OUT,ShopRobot:O.Data[0],52);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copy strings from Fanuc Karel Format to AB Format

Last (most recent) Alarm]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(ShopRobot.IN.lastAlarmData[1],ShopRobot.lastAlarm.LEN)COP(ShopRobot.IN.lastAlarmData[4],ShopRobot.lastAlarm.DATA[0],100);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Program Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(ShopRobot.IN.progStatusData[1],ShopRobot.programStatus.LEN)COP(ShopRobot.IN.progStatusData[4],ShopRobot.programStatus.DATA[0],100);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/// Run Robot Control AOI ///]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[FanucRobot(ShopRobotCtrl,ShopRobotSeq,1,0,ShopRobot.OUT.UI,ShopRobot.IN.UO,1,ALLOWABLE_ALARMS,ShopRobot.lastAlarm);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
